🧾 Description:
The Color Changer is a simple interactive web project that allows users to change the background color of a webpage or a specific element by clicking a button. It’s great for learning DOM manipulation and event handling in JavaScript.

⚙️ Features:
Changes the background color to a random color or predefined list.

User interaction through a button click.

Optional: Display the current color code (e.g., #FF5733 or rgb(255, 87, 51)).

🛠 Technologies Used:
HTML: For structuring the page and button.

CSS: For styling the layout and text.

JavaScript: For generating and applying colors dynamically.

🚀 How It Works:
User clicks the "Change Color" button.

JavaScript generates a random color (hex or rgb).

The color is applied to the page background (or another element).

Optionally, the new color code is displayed on the screen.

